{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And he takes up his discourse.</b> The meaning: he raised his voice in his discourse. And משל is like כנחלים נטיו (Numbers 24:6, \"they flow like streams\")." "<b>Discourse.</b> A thing, as in וינאמו (Numbers 23:7, \"and they discoursed\"). נאם: one says that the meaning of שומע (Numbers 24:4,16, \"hearing\") is also that he sees a thing that is clear and close to the mind — which is the way of prophecy in a dream, as the words of Eliphaz: תמונה לנגד עיני דממה וקול אשמע (Job 4:16, \"a figure before my eyes — silence, and a voice I hear\")." "<b>Whose eye is shut.</b> It has no parallel; rather its meaning is according to its context, the opposite of סתום (closed). And one says that Balaam had only one eye, and this is the way of derash."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {2 "'It has no parallel' translates אין לו אחר, reading אחר for the printed אח; alternatively, 'it has no brother' = no cognate verse, rendered idiomatically."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:19:18.648185581Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}